<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mularaja</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 941–996</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mularaja was the founder of the Chaulukya, or Solanki, dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patan-gujarat">Anahilavada</a> (Patan) from about 941 to 996. By tradition the nephew of the last Chavda king, he seized the throne around 942 and built a kingdom across northern Gujarat, fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chahamanas</a> of Shakambhari and the rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a>. His dynasty ruled Gujarat until 1244.</p></div>
